{
  "@context": "https://openvex.dev/ns/v0.2.0",
  "@id": "https://openvex.dev/docs/public/vex-report-updater-operator-trivy",
  "author": "Deckhouse <contact@deckhouse.io>",
  "version": 2,
  "statements": [
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-54448",
        "description": "Trivy: Helm chart tar bomb causes OOM via unbounded io.ReadAll in parser",
        "name": "CVE-2026-54448",
        "aliases": [ "GHSA-q3fv-x8vg-qqm4", "GO-2026-5983" ]
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/aquasecurity/trivy@v0.55.2"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_present",
      "impact_statement": "Trivy's custom Helm-chart (.tgz) tar unpacker reads entries via io.ReadAll with no size limit prior to 0.71.0, allowing a decompression-bomb DoS. Deckhouse Kubernetes Platform is not affected as operator-trivy report-updater only imports github.com/aquasecurity/trivy/pkg/fanal/types for shared type definitions - it never invokes Trivy's artifact/Helm-chart scanning or tar-unpacking code, so the vulnerable code path is not reachable from this binary.",
      "timestamp": "2026-08-13T00:00:00Z"
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-55092",
        "description": "Trivy: path traversal via a crafted vulnerability database or another OCI artifact",
        "name": "CVE-2026-55092"
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/aquasecurity/trivy@v0.55.2"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_present",
      "impact_statement": "When Trivy unpacks an OCI artifact pulled from a registry, such as its vulnerability database, it writes each entry at the path recorded in the artifact without checking that the path stays inside the destination directory, so a crafted artifact can write files outside the cache. Reaching the defect requires calling the artifact download and unpack code of Trivy. The report-updater binary links from Trivy only pkg/fanal/types and pkg/digest, the type definitions it shares with the report format of the operator (see internal/web/hook/trivy_types.go); go list -deps lists no other Trivy package, so the vulnerable code is not compiled into the image. The report-updater downloads no vulnerability database: it serves a webhook that rewrites reports the operator has already produced, and the one OCI artifact it does pull is fetched with oras.land/oras-go/v2, which this advisory does not cover.",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-23T12:00:00Z"
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-63328",
        "description": "Trivy: path traversal in the plugin manager allows arbitrary file write",
        "name": "CVE-2026-63328"
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:golang/github.com/aquasecurity/trivy@v0.55.2"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_present",
      "impact_statement": "The Trivy plugin manager installs a plugin from a remote source and extracts its archive without validating the entry paths, so a crafted plugin can write files anywhere the process can write. Reaching the defect requires an explicit plugin installation, which in Trivy is driven by the trivy plugin command. The report-updater binary links from Trivy only pkg/fanal/types and pkg/digest, the type definitions it shares with the report format of the operator (see internal/web/hook/trivy_types.go); go list -deps lists no other Trivy package, so the vulnerable code is not compiled into the image. The report-updater has no command line interface and no plugin support, and it installs nothing at runtime.",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-23T12:00:00Z"
    }
  ],
  "timestamp": "2026-08-13T00:00:00Z",
  "last_updated": "2026-09-23T12:00:00Z"
}
